Orca Wallet
===========

A simple Ethereum wallet implementation written for learning and experimentation.

Orca Wallet allows users to create new wallets, import existing wallets,
manage accounts, and interact with the Ethereum blockchain. It supports
sending and receiving ETH and ERC-20 tokens through Ethereum-compatible
networks.

This project is primarily intended for educational purposes and as a
personal software project. It demonstrates concepts involved in blockchain
wallet development, cryptographic key management, transaction handling,
and Ethereum RPC communication.


A. PROJECT HISTORY
==================

Orca Wallet was created as a personal project to explore Ethereum wallet
architecture and blockchain application development.

The project was developed to understand how cryptocurrency wallets work,
including:

    - Private key generation and wallet management
    - Ethereum account handling
    - Transaction creation and signing
    - ERC-20 token interaction
    - Blockchain RPC communication
    - Backend API design and database management

Orca Wallet is not intended to compete with production cryptocurrency
wallet applications. It is a learning-oriented implementation designed
to explore the technologies and engineering practices behind blockchain
software.


B. FEATURES
===========

Wallet Management
-----------------

    - Create new Ethereum wallets
    - Import existing wallets
    - Manage multiple wallet accounts
    - View wallet addresses


Ethereum Support
----------------

    - Connect to Ethereum-compatible networks
    - Check ETH balances
    - Send ETH transactions
    - Track transaction status


ERC-20 Token Support
--------------------

    - View ERC-20 token balances
    - Send ERC-20 token transactions
    - Interact with token smart contracts


Authentication & Backend
------------------------

    - User account management
    - OTP email verification
    - Secure API communication
    - Transaction history storage


C. TECHNOLOGIES USED
====================

Programming Languages
---------------------

    - TypeScript


Frontend
--------

    - Next.js (https://nextjs.org/)
    - Tailwind CSS (https://tailwindcss.com/)
    - shadcn/ui (https://ui.shadcn.com/)


Backend
-------

    - Node.js (https://nodejs.org/)
    - Express.js (https://expressjs.com/)
    - JSON Web Tokens (https://www.npmjs.com/package/jsonwebtoken)
    - Bcrypt (https://www.npmjs.com/package/bcrypt)
    - Redis (https://redis.io/)
    - Resend (https://resend.com/)


Database
--------

    - MongoDB Atlas (https://www.mongodb.com/cloud/atlas)


Database Toolkit
----------------

    - Prisma v6.19.0 (https://www.prisma.io/)


Blockchain
----------

    - ethers.js (Ethereum JavaScript library) (https://docs.ethers.org/v6/)
    - Alchemy (https://www.alchemy.com/)


D. GETTING STARTED
==================

Prerequisites
-------------

Before running Orca Wallet, make sure you have installed:

    - Node.js (https://nodejs.org/)


Installation
------------

Clone the repository:

    git clone https://github.com/wxrayut/orca-wallet

Navigate to the project directory:

    cd orca-wallet


Environment Configuration
-------------------------

Create an environment file:

    Rename `.env.example` to `.env` in the backend directory.

Configure the required environment variables:

    ORCA_ENCRYPTION_KEY=<YOUR_32_CHARACTER_ENCRYPTION_KEY>

    JWT_ACCESS_SECRET=<YOUR_64_CHARACTER_HEX_STRING>

    RPC_API_KEY=<YOUR_ALCHEMY_API_KEY>

    RESEND_API_KEY=<YOUR_RESEND_API_KEY>

    RESEND_SENDER_EMAIL=<YOUR_RESEND_SENDER_EMAIL>

    ADMIN_USERNAME="<YOUR_ADMIN_USERNAME>"

    ADMIN_EMAIL="<YOUR_ADMIN_EMAIL>"

    ADMIN_PASSWORD="<YOUR_ADMIN_PASSWORD>"


MongoDB Atlas Setup
-------------------

Orca Wallet uses MongoDB Atlas for storing application data.

Make sure a MongoDB Atlas cluster is available before starting the application.

Configure the database connection in your environment file:

    DATABASE_URL=mongodb+srv://<USERNAME>:<PASSWORD>@cluster0.cgdqoii.mongodb.net/<DATABASE_NAME>?retryWrites=true&w=majority&appName=Cluster0


Redis Setup (WSL)
-----------------

For development environments, Redis can be run inside
Windows Subsystem for Linux (WSL).

    sudo service redis-server start

Verify Redis is running:

    redis-cli ping

Expected output:

    PONG

The application can connect to Redis using:

    REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379


Running the Application
-----------------------

Install dependencies:

    npm install


Build shared package:

    npm run build --workspace=@orca-wallet/shared


Prisma Database Setup:

    # Navigate to the backend directory
    cd apps/backend

    # Run Prisma setup to create the database schema and apply migrations
    npm run prisma:setup

    # Return to the root directory
    cd ../..


Start the application:

    npx turbo dev


E. PROJECT STRUCTURE
====================

The project is organized into several components:

    apps/
        frontend/
            frontend application built with Next.js, Tailwind CSS and shadcn/ui

        backend/
            backend API built with Node.js and Express.js

    packages/
        shared/
            shared libraries and utilities


F. SECURITY NOTICE
==================

Orca Wallet is a personal learning project created for educational and experimental purposes.

This project has not undergone a professional security audit and should not be considered 
production-ready. The implementation may contain security vulnerabilities, design limitations, 
or other issues that could result in loss of funds or sensitive information.

Do not use Orca Wallet to store real cryptocurrency assets or private keys with real value.

If you plan to use this project in a production environment, you should perform your own security 
review and consider implementing additional security measures, such as:

    - Professional security audits
    - Proper key management solutions
    - Hardware security modules (HSM) or secure key storage
    - Strong encryption practices
    - Rate limiting and abuse prevention
    - Input validation and sanitization
    - Secure authentication mechanisms
    - Comprehensive logging and monitoring
    - Regular dependency and vulnerability checks
    - Penetration testing

The security level of this project can be improved depending on your requirements and intended use case.


